        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">viell. nur Verschreibung</hi> [<hi rend="italic">oder unbelegte Metathese</hi>] <hi rend="italic">für</hi> freome</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">perhaps merely a miswriting [or an unattested metathesis] for freome</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.oe.4-3" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">321</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a. i. <hi rend="italic">HDiLb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a. i. HDiLb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">321</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">clamationem <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">clamationem S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">321</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">321</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">expurg. <hi rend="italic">HLb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">expurg. HLb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">321</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt LbS</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in LbS</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.oe.9-3" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">321</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uo. <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> di. <hi rend="italic">HDi</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uo. Cb; di. HDi</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">321</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">he <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">he S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">321</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">pere <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">pere Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">204</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt durch Hn 34, 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used by Hn 34, 7</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">204</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">feore</hi> las wohl Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>, da <hi rend="italic">vita</hi> Hn, wie Inst, gemäss der Quelle (III Eg 4, auch EGu 12), also vielleicht aus Marginalie des Archetyps; <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. Einl. 3.—Für <hi rend="italic">fremu</hi> ist die Schreibung <hi rend="italic">freom</hi>- (durch Toller zu <hi rend="italic">fremian</hi>, -<hi rend="italic">mung</hi>, <hi rend="italic">freomlic</hi>) bezeugt; -<hi rend="italic">a</hi> in B ist spät für -<hi rend="italic">e</hi>. Ob aber <hi rend="italic">feorme</hi> nur Metathese für <hi rend="italic">freome</hi> sein kann? Wahrscheinlicher lag A im Kopf die Alliterationsformel <hi rend="italic">feoh ⁊ feorm</hi> Toller 280 I; Becwæð 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> probably read <hi rend="italic">feore</hi>, since Hn, like Inst, has <hi rend="italic">vita</hi>, in accordance with the source (III Eg 4, also EGu 12); thus perhaps from a marginal note in the archetype; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> Introduction 3.—For <hi rend="italic">fremu</hi> the spelling <hi rend="italic">freom</hi>- is attested (by Toller under <hi rend="italic">fremian</hi>, -<hi rend="italic">mung</hi>, <hi rend="italic">freomlic</hi>); -<hi rend="italic">a</hi> in B is late for -<hi rend="italic">e</hi>. But can <hi rend="italic">feorme</hi> be merely a metathesis of <hi rend="italic">freome</hi>? More probably A had in mind the alliterative formula <hi rend="italic">feoh ⁊ feorm</hi> Toller 280 I; Becwæð 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">204</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">intentator</hi> Q, wohl aus <hi rend="italic">intento</hi> ‘gerichtlich bedrohen’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">intentator</hi> Q, probably from <hi rend="italic">intento</hi> ‘to threaten in court’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_16.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">him</hi> als Acc. mittelengl., bei B öfter; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi> 111 Sp. 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">him</hi> as acc. is Middle English, frequent in B; <hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi> 111 col. 1</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_16.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. III Edg. 4; Hn. 34, 7.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_16.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The texts show three different readings of this phrase, viz. (1) <hi rend="italic">feo o. freoma</hi>, B, cf. G (<hi rend="italic">o. freme</hi>), Q (<hi rend="italic">pecunia vel commodo</hi>), Cons. (<hi rend="italic">censu aut commodo</hi>); (2) <hi rend="italic">feo o. feorh</hi>, Ld, cf. Inst. (<hi rend="italic">pecuniam aut vitam</hi>); (3) <hi rend="italic">feo o. feorme</hi>, A. Liebermann takes <hi rend="italic">freoma</hi>, B, as a late form of <hi rend="italic">freme</hi> (see Toller, <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> p. 264, <hi rend="italic">s.v.</hi> <hi rend="italic">fremu</hi>), and suggests that the scribe of A had in mind the alliterative phrase <hi rend="italic">feoh ⁊ feorm</hi> (see Toller, <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> p. 213, <hi rend="italic">s.v.</hi> <hi rend="italic">feorm</hi>). Here as in III Edg. 4 (see note) I have adopted the reading <hi rend="italic">feo o. freme</hi> (<hi rend="italic">freoma</hi>).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_16.robnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">182</biblScope></bibl><label>freoma</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">freme</hi> G; <hi rend="italic">feorme</hi> A; <hi rend="italic">feorh</hi> Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_16.robnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">182</biblScope></bibl><label>him</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hine</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
